cff-version: 1.2.0
title: NetScope — Internet Experience Intelligence for your terminal
message: >-
  If you use NetScope in research or teaching, please cite it using
  this metadata (the GitHub "Cite this repository" button reads this
  file).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abolfazl
    family-names: Ranjbaran
    alias: Abolfazlrwm
    website: "https://github.com/Abolfazlrwm"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Abolfazlrwm/netscope"
abstract: >-
  NetScope is a local-first network diagnostics CLI that turns raw
  probe measurements (ICMP, DNS, TCP, TLS, HTTP, traceroute,
  bandwidth) into evidence-based answers about whose fault a bad
  connection is — the local network, the ISP, or the destination
  service. It learns a personal statistical baseline per target, keeps
  a "drift watch" over recent history windows, refuses to report
  missing probes as healthy, and exports self-contained evidence
  reports as markdown, HTML, CSV and Prometheus metrics. All data stays
  in a local SQLite database.
keywords:
  - network-diagnostics
  - latency
  - packet-loss
  - jitter
  - internet-health
  - evidence-based-diagnosis
  - cli
